# Docker build context — allowlist, not blocklist.
#
# The repository carries a local `build/` tree (hundreds of MB of objects, Qt
# DLLs and a .pdb), `node_modules/`, generated graph output and the whole `.git`
# history. A blocklist would have to be updated every time one of those grows a
# sibling; excluding everything and naming the three directories the image
# actually reads cannot drift.
*

!backend
!frontend
!docker

# …minus what lives inside them and never belongs in an image: local build
# trees, the frontend's dev tooling and the IDE's scratch files. cmake --install
# already strips node_modules & friends from the staged frontend, but keeping
# them out of the context is what makes the upload fast and the layer cache
# stable.
backend/build
backend/.qtcreator
backend/tests/build
frontend/node_modules
frontend/coverage
frontend/build
**/.DS_Store
